/// is the literal `+0.0f`. Every alternative was actively refuted:
///
/// | candidate | killed by | oracle | candidate |
/// |---|---|---|---|
/// | `max <= 0 ? 0 : d/max`      | `(-1, -1, -2)`            | `-1`     | `0`      |
/// | `max > 0 ? d/max : 0`       | `(-1, -1, -1)`            | `-0`     | `0`      |
/// | `max == 0 ? delta : d/max`  | `(0, 0, -1)`              | `0`      | `1`      |
/// | `delta == 0 ? 0 : d/max`    | `(0, 0, -1)`              | `0`      | `inf`    |
/// | `max == min ? 0 : d/max`    | `(0, 0, -1)`              | `0`      | `inf`    |
/// | `max == 0 ? -0.0f : d/max`  | `(-0.0, -1, -2)`          | `0`      | `-0`     |
/// | no guard at all (`d/max`)   | `(0, 0, 0)`               | `0`      | `-nan`   |
/// | `1 - min/max`               | `(0, -0.0, inf)`          | `-nan`   | `1`      |
/// | `(max>0 \|\| max<0) ? d/max : 0` | `(NaN, 0, 0)`        | `nan`    | `0`      |
/// | `delta * (1.0f / max)`      | `(0.851135075, 2.41347075, 0.246790618)` | `0.897744` | `0.897745` |
